# vigil-lock PAM service: a named hook, not a policy. vigil only runs the
# conversation; WHAT authenticates (password, fingerprint, anything PAM
# can express) is operator configuration. By default the lock behaves
# exactly like login. Edit this file to give the lockscreen its own rules.
#
# Only the auth phase: a locker re-authenticates an already-logged-in
# user; account validity was settled at login (and pam_unix account
# needs privileges a user-service context does not have).
auth     include   login
